# No live mail, no secrets

- Do not call real SMTP to verify changes. Use dry-run, `mail.batch-enabled=false`, and mocked `JavaMailSender` in tests.
- Do not put `MAIL_PASSWORD` or App Passwords in source, commits, or README examples (keep placeholders).
- Do not commit `application-local.properties` or `.env` (gitignored).
- I1 (rotate leaked Gmail App Password) is the user’s Google Account action. Do not rewrite git history unless they explicitly ask.

```text
# ❌ BAD — tests or run that send to a real spreadsheet
MAIL_BATCH_ENABLED=true MAIL_DRY_RUN=false mvn spring-boot:run

# ✅ GOOD — batch off or dry-run; tests mock JavaMailSender
```
